/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  pairLookup03_provenance_stale_seal
  ==================================

  WHAT IT IS.  Witness of the PROVENANCE LINE every lookup card carries (DEV.md
  4c C227 (a)) (the card carries a provenance line and the JSON a `catalogue` object).

  THIS CASE: SEALED, and its manifest names Choupo-2607 -- a legitimate old
  seal (the catalogue identity a seal records is the catalogue as it stood
  when the case was frozen; CATALOGUE.dat explains why 394 manifests keep
  that name) -- while the installation is Choupo-2608.  The lookups still read
  the installation, so the card is from a release that is NOT the case's own,
  and the provenance line SAYS so: `case sealed Choupo-2607; differs "..."`.
  The result JSON carries the same fact as `releaseDiffers true`.
  Pinned: the tier word, the card bytes.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
